<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prabu Geusan Ulun Museum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prabu-geusan-ulun">Prabu Geusan Ulun</a> Museum is a museum in the former regents' palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumedang">Sumedang</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, named after the 16th-century ruler of Sumedang Larang. It holds the heirlooms of the Sumedang ruling family, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binokasih">Binokasih crown</a> traditionally said to have come from the Sunda Kingdom, together with weapons, gamelan instruments and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>.</p></div>
